      "message": "test(verify): pin the in-cell kappa bound and the backstop's span floor\n\nThe #1313 safety review found three mutations no test caught:\n- dropping `+ kappa` from a turn cell's rim dip,\n- deleting the backstop column's span-floor line,\n- reverting the backstop column to the whole radius.\n\nturn_cells::tests::a_cell_straddling_a_flat_pose_reads_the_flat_rim\n(B 60 -> 120, radius 100, 0.5 long) convicts a stock post that the\nflat band dips 1.25 um into, and checks every cell against a dense pose\nscan. The sweep backstop pin (A 100 -> 260, a hidden post at (5, 0))\nasserts the exact verdict at -53 (convicted) and -58 (clean) and the\nreading -L - R*sin 40.\n\nRefs #1313\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
